  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Thrown by <see cref="T:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedClient" /> when a reset marker is discovered on
            the change feed and the effective reset policy is
            <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedResetPolicy.ThrowOnReset" />.
            </summary>
    <remarks>
            A reset marker signals that log-sequence continuity has been broken (for example, by a
            HardFailover or classic account migration). Batched APIs
            (<see cref="M:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedClient.GetChanges(System.Nullable{System.DateTimeOffset},System.Nullable{System.DateTimeOffset})" />
            and <see cref="M:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedClient.GetChangesBetweenSnapshots(System.String,System.String)" />) fail
            fast before yielding any events when the requested range crosses a reset boundary; the
            streaming <see cref="M:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedClient.GetChanges" /> overloads stop at the reset
            boundary. Inspect <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedResetException.ResetEvent" /> to recover reset context (id, time, account,
            share, reason) and drive the appropriate recovery path (typically a full re-baseline).
            </remarks>
  </Docs>
